merge, create derivative works of, and distribute the Covered Material, in
source or other form. Distribution may be standalone or part of a bundle,
provided that it complies with section 4.

4. No monetized distribution
---------------------------

You must not sell, rent, or otherwise monetize distribution of or access to
the Covered Material, including modified versions and portions incorporated
into other works. You must not include or deliver it as part of a monetized
addon collection, bundle, installer, launcher, update service, or other offering.

Monetization includes direct or indirect monetary or other material benefit
connected with providing, promoting, or maintaining that distribution or access,
whether received by You or another person acting on your behalf. In particular,
the prohibition covers:

* Purchase prices, subscriptions, paid memberships and paid private channels,
  including Boosty, Patreon and equivalent services.
* Payments or donations required for downloads, access, early access, updates
  or other distribution-related advantages.
* Advertising, sponsorship, referral revenue and voluntary donations solicited
  or accepted to fund or reward distribution or maintenance of the offering,
  even when its downloads are available to everyone without payment.
* Charges described as payment for compilation, packaging, installation,
  configuration, support or another service when the transaction includes
  delivery of or access to the Covered Material or a bundle containing it.

The prohibition applies even if the Covered Material is described as a free
component, gift or bonus, if the fee is attributed to other components or
services, or if an installer downloads it separately instead of bundling it.
Renaming or modifying it does not remove these conditions. Unrelated income
of a distributor does not by itself constitute monetization under this section.

